    query: {'description': 'The email of the contacts to search for.', 'type': 'string'}

get_current_day: Returns the current day in ISO format, e.g. '2022-01-01'. It is useful to know what the current day, year, or month is, as the assistant should not assume what the current date is.

search_calendar_events: Searches calendar events that match the given query in the tile or the description. If provided, filters events by date.
  parameters:
    query: {'description': 'The query string to search for in event titles and descriptions.', 'type': 'string'}
    date: {'description': 'The date for which to search events. Must be in format YYYY-MM-DD. If `null`, searches all events.', 'type': 'string'}

get_day_calendar_events: Returns the appointments for the given `day`. Returns a list of dictionaries with informations about each meeting.
  parameters:
    day: {'description': 'The day for which to return the appointments. Must be in format YYYY-MM-DD.', 'type': 'string'}

create_calendar_event: Creates a new calendar event with the given details and adds it to the calendar. It also sends an email to the participants with the event details.
  parameters:
    title: {'description': 'The title of the event.', 'type': 'string'}
    start_time: {'description': 'The start time of the event. Must be in format YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM.', 'type': 'string'}
    end_time: {'description': 'The end time of the event. Must be in format YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM.', 'type': 'string'}
    description: {'description': 'The description of the event.', 'type': 'string'}
    participants: {'description': "The list of participants' email addresses. If `null`, no participants are set. The calendar owner's email address is always included..", 'type': 'string'}
    location: {'description': 'The location of the event. If `null`, no location is set.', 'type': 'string'}

cancel_calendar_event: Cancels the event with the given `event_id`. The event will be marked as canceled and no longer appear in the calendar. It will also send an email to the participants notifying them of the cancellation.
  parameters:
    event_id: {'description': 'The ID of the event to cancel.', 'type': 'string'}

reschedule_calendar_event: Reschedules the event with the given `event_id` to the new start and end times. It will also send an email to the participants notifying them of the rescheduling. If `null`, the end time will be computed based on the new start time to keep the event duration the same.
  parameters:
    event_id: {'description': 'The ID of the event to reschedule.', 'type': 'string'}
    new_start_time: {'description': 'The new start time of the event. Must be in format YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM.', 'type': 'string'}
    new_end_time: {'description': 'The new end time of the event. Must be in format YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM.', 'type': 'string'}

add_calendar_event_participants: Adds the given `participants` to the event with the given `event_id`. It will also email the new participants notifying them of the event.
  parameters:
    event_id: {'description': 'The ID of the event to add participants to.', 'type': 'string'}
    participants: {'description': "The list of participants' email addresses to add to the event.", 'type': 'string'}

append_to_file: Append content to a file in the cloud drive.
  parameters:
    file_id: {'description': 'The ID of the file to append content to.', 'type': 'string'}
    content: {'description': 'The content to append to the file.', 'type': 'string'}

search_files_by_filename: Get a file from a cloud drive by its filename. It returns a list of files. Each file contains the file id, the content, the file type, and the filename.
  parameters:
    filename: {'description': 'The name of the file to retrieve.', 'type': 'string'}

create_file: Create a new file in the cloud drive.
  parameters:
    filename: {'description': 'The name of the file to create.', 'type': 'string'}
    content: {'description': 'The content of the file to create.', 'type': 'string'}

delete_file: Delete a file from the cloud drive by its filename. It returns the file that was deleted.
  parameters:
    file_id: {'description': 'The name of the file to delete.', 'type': 'string'}

get_file_by_id: Get a file from a cloud drive by its ID.
  parameters:
    file_id: {'description': 'The ID of the file to retrieve.', 'type': 'string'}

list_files: Retrieve all files in the cloud drive.

share_file: Share a file with a user.
  parameters:
    file_id: {'description': 'The ID of the file to share.', 'type': 'string'}
    email: {'description': 'The email of the user to share the file with.', 'type': 'string'}
    permission: {'description': 'The permission level to grant the user.', 'type': 'string'}

search_files: Search for files in the cloud drive by content.
  parameters:
    query: {'description': 'The string to search for in the files.', 'type': 'string'}
